  "body": "## Purpose\nC256 observes geometry and sampled motion, but it does not independently establish ownership. C257 adds a finite ownership component for the existing C253/C210 family without changing runtime or released behavior.\n\n## Change and behavior\n- Derive immediate lifecycle ownership from authoritative `.ok` declarations, including module visibility and keyed generated parts.\n- Independently read actual GLB ownership metadata and compare repeated identity/source claims.\n- Keep source facts, untrusted artifact claims, consistency checks and historical admission as separate API boundaries.\n- Preserve initial failures, corrections and exact review evidence in `docs/engineering/localized-repair-c257/`.\n\n## Exact review and checks\nPublished source: `3222fc9a61e69986f4647e65ae626bd2d21e5f95`.\nReviewed tree: `0dc9462a55f7b3d48337d0506cb43215b87f0d87`.\nScientific author: `499a19d030a06609564390877a596d53dc015a7a`; final author closure: `c827c76c49eed793f009d9245fbc633f6a4169b5`.\n\n23 authored methods and 107 independent controls pass, with separate structural and integration review. Focused checks pass C256's 29 methods, C255's 31 methods, C253's 14 files/three cases, and 29 preserved documentation sources/233 sections/5,484 links. All existing runtime, fixture, schema and workflow paths are unchanged. Fresh resulting-main checks follow the merge under the verified integration lease.\n\n## Limits and closure\nThis is an ownership component only. Following, hinges, complete semantic qualification, revision authenticity, source rebuilds, native routes and model trials remain unqualified. Known historical failures and release gates are unchanged.\n\nScope #243 remains open until the final handoff archive is independently restored and its saved delivery is confirmed. The next feature is a separate step. Integration owner: `c257-root-da3bfd223c61-20261117`, lease parent `a934f237368ee531d0f96c101994cbdd467e09c6`.",
